{number: 107}
{title: Abide with Me}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
A-[Eb] bide with [Bb7] me: fast [Eb] falls the [Ab] eventide;
The [Eb] darkness [Cm] deepens; [F7] Lord, with me a-[Bb7] bide:
When [Eb] other [Bb7] helpers [Eb] fail and [Ab] comforts flee,
Help [Eb] of the [Cm] helpless, [Eb] O a-[Bb7] bide with [Eb] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Swift [Eb] to its [Bb7] close ebbs [Eb] out life's [Ab] little day;
Earth's [Eb] joys grow [Cm] dim, its [F7] glories pass a-[Bb7] way;
Change [Eb] and de-[Bb7] cay in [Eb] all a-[Ab] round I see;
O [Eb] Thou who [Cm] changest not, [Eb] a-[Bb7] bide with [Eb] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
I [Eb] need Thy [Bb7] presence [Eb] every [Ab] passing hour;
What [Eb] but Thy [Cm] grace can [F7] foil the tempter's [Bb7] pow'r?
Who, [Eb] like Thy-[Bb7] self, my [Eb] guide and [Ab] stay can be?
Through [Eb] cloud and [Cm] sunshine, [Eb] Lord, a-[Bb7] bide with [Eb] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Hold [Eb] Thou Thy [Bb7] cross be-[Eb] fore my [Ab] closing eyes;
Shine [Eb] through the [Cm] gloom and [F7] point me to the [Bb7] skies:
Heav'n's [Eb] morning [Bb7] breaks, and [Eb] earth's vain [Ab] shadows flee;
In [Eb] life, in [Cm] death, O [Eb] Lord, a-[Bb7] bide with [Eb] me.
{end_of_verse}
